    },
    {
      "id": "279-2",
      "citation": "Section 279(2)",
      "unit_type": "subsection",
      "parent_id": "279",
      "section_id": "279",
      "section_number": "279",
      "title": "Income escaping assessment.",
      "text": "For the purposes of assessment or reassessment or recomputation under sub-section (1), the Assessing Officer may assess or reassess the income in respect of any issue, which has escaped assessment, and such issue comes to his notice subsequently in the course of the proceedings under this section, irrespective of the fact that the provisions of section 281 have not been complied with.",
      "retrieval_text": "Chapter XVI PROCEDURE FOR ASSESSMENT Chapter XVI, Division A Procedure for assessment Section 279 Income escaping assessment. Section 279(2): For the purposes of assessment or reassessment or recomputation under sub-section (1), the Assessing Officer may assess or reassess the income in respect of any issue, which has escaped assessment, and such issue comes to his notice subsequently in the course of the proceedings under this section, irrespective of the fact that the provisions of section 281 have not been complied with.",
